{"task": "Prove exactly this local conditional obligation using the supplied NL route. Return only the tactic body through submit_transition. All displayed parameter and input proof binders are already in context.", "packet": {"version": 2, "contract_sha256": "3575d5d75c1eb2aaf8b92e3182b02e09afba2fd0f4d1ab9e569e2cc16c872495", "header": "import Mathlib

open scoped ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

abbrev YuiEucl (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
def YuiI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1
def YuiSnoc {n : ℕ} (x : YuiEucl n) (t : ℝ) : YuiEucl (n + 1) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.snoc (fun i => x i) t)
def YuiHead {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : YuiEucl n :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i : Fin n => z i.castSucc)
def YuiLast {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)
def YuiCylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (YuiEucl n)) : Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)) :=
  {z | YuiHead z ∈ E ∧ YuiLast z ∈ YuiI}
noncomputable def YuiCost {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] {ι : Type*}
    (s : ℝ) (U : ι → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s
def YuiCover {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X)
    (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop :=
  A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ
noncomputable def YuiContent {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : YuiCover δ A U), YuiCost s U
noncomputable def YuiMeasure {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), YuiContent s δ A
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "E", "type": "Set (YuiEucl n)"}], "representation": "Use EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)=PiLp 2 (constant ℝ), indexed by Fin n, with its native L2 metric and Borel structure; n is a natural ambient dimension including 0. YuiSnoc appends a real coordinate and YuiHead/YuiLast recover it; YuiCylinder E is defined by these coordinates directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)). T003 checks the coordinate inverse and Euclidean distance identities used by all cylinder arguments, so there is no max-product metric or unproved metric replacement. The interval remains Set.Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam, YuiCost, YuiContent and YuiMeasure take values in ℝ≥0∞; ^ with a real exponent is ENNReal.rpow. The supremum over a nonempty witness equals ediam^s and over an empty witness equals zero, giving the prescribed empty-cover convention even at exponent zero. All uses of Hausdorff content or normalization are guarded by s>0 and δ>0. Cover sequences enumerate countable covers with empty padding; the positive-diameter construction uses a subset of ℕ to avoid duplicating finite nonempty families. dimH is native, defined as the supremum of nonnegative exponents with infinite native unnormalized Hausdorff measure; its nonnegative extended codomain gives dimH empty=0. Positive real exponents are embedded by ENNReal.ofReal only with the relevant positivity; D remains dimH E in ℝ≥0∞ and its toReal value is used only downstream of T005's finiteness. Nat casts of n and constants are finite ENNReal values. Lebesgue measure/integrals in the slicing and interval workers are volume on ℝ and the nonnegative lintegral. All five M facts are supplied by direct pinned Mathlib use, not additional premises. Background notes remain optional node-local references. N outputs are unchanged; auxiliary T001 exposes the uniform metric-space normalization calculation already used in S001 so both Euclidean and real-interval instances can share it.", "inputs": [{"id": "T003", "binder": "h_T003", "type": "∀ k : ℕ, (∀ (x : YuiEucl k) (t : ℝ), YuiHead (YuiSnoc x t) = x ∧ YuiLast (YuiSnoc x t) = t) ∧ (∀ z : YuiEucl (k + 1), YuiSnoc (YuiHead z) (YuiLast z) = z) ∧ (∀ (x y : YuiEucl k) (t u : ℝ), dist (YuiSnoc x t) (YuiSnoc y u) = Real.sqrt ((dist x y) ^ 2 + |t-u| ^ 2)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiHead (n := k)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiLast (n := k))"}, {"id": "T007", "binder": "h_T007", "type": "1 ≤ n → ∀ q : ℝ, dimH E < ENNReal.ofReal q → ∀ r ε : ℝ, 0 < r → r ≤ 1 → 0 < ε → ∃ (T : Set ℕ) (U : T → Set (YuiEucl n)), E ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ (∀ i, (U i).Nonempty ∧ 0 < Metric.ediam (U i) ∧ Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal r) ∧ YuiCost q U < ENNReal.ofReal ε"}], "target": "1 ≤ n → ∀ q : ℝ, dimH E < ENNReal.ofReal q → ∀ r ε : ℝ, 0 < r → r ≤ 1 → 0 < ε → ∃ W : ℕ → Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)), YuiCover (Real.sqrt 2 * r) (YuiCylinder E) W ∧ YuiCost (q + 1) W < ENNReal.ofReal (2 * (Real.sqrt 2) ^ (q + 1) * ε)", "explanation": "Apply T007 at the given q,r,ε. For each positive diameter r_i partition I into ceil(1/r_i) intervals and append them to U_i. The finite multiplicity is ≤2/r_i, and T003 gives Euclidean mesh ≤sqrt(2)*r_i. Group the nonnegative countable sum to bound (q+1)-cost by 2*(sqrt 2)^(q+1) times the original q-cost; all powers use real exponents and finite positive diameters. Enumerate the countable union of finite families with empty padding. The conclusion eliminates the private U, indices and partitions.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S012", "text": "Choose U from F002; set r_i=diam(U_i) and N_i=ceil(1/r_i). Partition I into N_i equal closed intervals of length 1/N_i≤r_i. Since 0<r_i≤r≤1, N_i≤1/r_i+1≤2/r_i. Let W be the family of products of U_i with these intervals. It is countable, being a countable union of finite families, and covers F. For any two points in a member of W, the squared Euclidean distance is at most r_i^2+r_i^2. Thus each member has diameter ≤sqrt(2) r_i≤sqrt(2) r."}, {"id": "S013", "text": "Using F003 and q>0, the total (q+1)-cost of W is at most sum_i N_i(sqrt(2) r_i)^(q+1) ≤ 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1) sum_i r_i^q < 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1) epsilon. All terms are nonnegative, so termwise inequalities and the countable grouping are valid even before finiteness is known; the last strict inequality supplies finiteness. Since r and epsilon were arbitrary and the private U does not occur in the assertion, this proves: for every r0 in (0,1] and every e0>0, F has a countable cover of mesh ≤sqrt(2) r0 and (q+1)-cost <2(sqrt(2))^(q+1)e0."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "1bf0b9c7347572e230e12960e1ad72681eb160b097abdd7fb42c849256a378a3", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R003.BG004", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For 0<t≤1, the integer m=ceil(1/t) is positive and satisfies 1/m≤t and m≤1/t+1≤2/t. A countable union of finite families is countable. If diam U=t and J is an interval of length at most t, then the Euclidean product U×J has diameter at most sqrt(2)t."}, {"id": "R003.BG005", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "Countable sums of nonnegative extended-real terms admit termwise comparison and regrouping over countable partitions. Also sum_{i≥0}2^{−i−2}=1/2. Consequently the singleton replacements in S002 cost at most epsilon/2, and the grouping of product-cover costs in S004 is valid before finiteness is established."}]}}
